* Methods and pointer indirection (2)

The equivalent thing happens in the reverse direction.

Functions that take a value argument must take a value of that specific type:

⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000001⟫Compile error!⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000002⟫while methods with value receivers take either a value or a pointer as the
receiver when they are called:

⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000003⟫

In this case, the method call ⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000004⟫p.Abs()⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000005⟫ is interpreted as ⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000006⟫(*p).Abs()⟪GTI18N_61a9cb84_000007⟫.

